---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Strategy & Advisory" description="Marketing strategy that serves your business strategy. Senior advisory from the principal who leads it.">

<!-- HERO -->
<section class="hero hero--sub section--indigo">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--light reveal">Layer 1 / Strategy &amp; Advisory</span>
    <h1>Marketing strategy that serves your business strategy</h1>
    <p class="lead">The foundation of everything. Before the budget is set, before the brief is written, before the tactics are chosen. A senior marketing partner sitting alongside you, reading the business clearly, and building a marketing strategy that delivers on what your business actually needs.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- WHAT'S INCLUDED -->
<section class="service-detail-layout">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="included-section">
      <h2 class="reveal">What's<br />included</h2>
      <ul class="included-list reveal d1">
        <li>Market and competitive analysis</li>
        <li>Brand positioning and strategy</li>
        <li>Marketing roadmap</li>
        <li>Messaging framework</li>
        <li>Capability assessment</li>
        <li>Strategic governance</li>
        <li>Planning oversight</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- WHO IT'S FOR -->
    <div class="who-section">
      <h2 class="reveal">Who it's for</h2>
      <div class="who-grid">
        <div class="who-card reveal">
          <h3>Businesses at inflection points</h3>
          <p>You're scaling, launching something new, or you've realised the marketing strategy that worked yesterday won't work for tomorrow.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="who-card reveal d1">
          <h3>Leaders who need perspective</h3>
          <p>You're too close to see clearly, and you need senior external judgment you can trust.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="who-card reveal d2">
          <h3>Businesses with capability but no strategy</h3>
          <p>You have good people doing good work, but nobody's holding the broader picture of where the marketing is meant to take the business.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- TESTIMONIALS -->
<section class="testimonials-section">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="reveal">What clients say</h2>
    <div class="testimonials-grid">
      <div class="testimonial-card reveal">
        <p>"The clarity Andrew brought was exactly what we needed. We had good people, but nobody was connecting the dots back to the business. Now we know what we're building toward, and everyone's aligned."</p>
        <cite>
          <strong>Client Name</strong>
          Title, Company
        </cite>
      </div>
      <div class="testimonial-card reveal d1">
        <p>"Having Andrew as a strategic guide has changed how we think about marketing. It's not about being busy; it's about being strategic. The difference shows up in our results."</p>
        <cite>
          <strong>Client Name</strong>
          Title, Company
        </cite>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- CTA -->
<section class="cta-band">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="cta-band__inner">
      <h2>Ready to build a strategy that <em>works</em>?</h2>
      <div class="cta-band__right">
        <span class="cta-band__email">hello@wearegreaterthan.co.nz</span>
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn--primary-dark">Book a discovery call <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

</BaseLayout>
